From 524f4c5f2bb8599a124543f9239cb564cbd4ddff Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stanley <stanley.chang@intel.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 13:13:21 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] acpi: ipu7: route one MAX96724 to CSI_A and CSI_B

Let one MAX96724 deserializer output to two IPU CSI-2 ports.
GMSL links A/B go to CSI_A (IPU port 0) and links C/D go to
CSI_B (IPU port 1). No driver change is needed.

- _des_common_max96724.asl: add an optional second CSI2Bus
  resource, enabled when the board defines DES_INTERNAL_PHY_2
  and DES_TO_MIPI_PORT_2.
- _ipu_dual_csi_ab.asl: new IPU0 fragment with port 0 and
  port 1 set to 2 data lanes each, so port 0 does not join
  port 1.
- max96724-servoss_d3_isx031.asl: DES0 uses PHY2 (port 6) to
  CSI_A and PHY3 (port 7) to CSI_B, C-PHY 2 trios.
- mc-setup.sh: support a DES with more than one output. Map
  links to outputs (default: link * nout / max_links), with
  DES_LINK_OUT="D:L:O ..." to override.
- acpi.json (ipu75xa): acpi-3 and acpi-4 use Intel IPU7 CSI2 1
  and ISYS Capture 10/11.

Tested on PTL (IPU7.5) with 4x ISX031.

Signed-off-by: Stanley <stanley.chang@intel.com>
---
 acpi/ipu7/_des_common_max96724.asl       |  17 +++
 acpi/ipu7/_ipu_dual_csi_ab.asl           |  48 ++++++
 acpi/ipu7/max96724-servoss_d3_isx031.asl |   8 +-
 config/acpi/ipu75xa/sensors/acpi.json    |  24 +--
 script/acpi/mc-setup.sh                  | 178 +++++++++++++++++------
 5 files changed, 215 insertions(+), 60 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 acpi/ipu7/_ipu_dual_csi_ab.asl

